technitium-console for Debian/Ubuntu
==============================

Files live in /usr/share/technitium-console, served by Technitium DNS
Server 15.5 or later via:

  DNS_SERVER_WEB_SERVICE_WWW_FOLDER_PATH=/usr/share/technitium-console

Restart the DNS service once after setting it. On Docker, mount this
folder (or a copy of it) read-only at the path the variable names; see
the upstream README "Docker" section.

Uninstalling this package removes the files but never touches the DNS
server's configuration: take the variable out (or unmount) and restart
the server once to go back to its stock console.

The one-line installer
(https://github.com/byGarcia/technitium-console#installing) remains the
recommended path on a live server: it finds the running service,
verifies what it serves, and can roll back. A copy is kept at
/usr/share/doc/technitium-console/install.sh.
